WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.202
-Our first guest directed,
co-wrote, and stars

00:00:03.202 --> 00:00:06.606
alongside Tiffany Haddish
in the new film "Here Today."

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:10.010
It is available now
on digital Blu-ray and DVD.

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:13.846
Here is the one,
the only Billy Crystal!

00:00:13.846 --> 00:00:14.914
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:18.117
That's what I'm talking about.
Yeah!

00:00:18.117 --> 00:00:19.318
Oh!

00:00:19.318 --> 00:00:21.053
Look at you.
-Finally.

00:00:21.053 --> 00:00:23.489
-Welcome back.
Billy, I'm so happy.

00:00:23.489 --> 00:00:26.058
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:00:26.058 --> 00:00:28.628
-Well, I wish
I actually was there, you know?

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:30.096
-Yeah, that's true.

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:33.499
-But, you know, at times there,
I'm a little afraid to fly.

00:00:33.499 --> 00:00:36.269
So, yeah, not about the COVID.

00:00:36.269 --> 00:00:38.471
The passengers. It's the...

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:39.973
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.973 --> 00:00:42.908
I mean, I actually called
for reservations, Jimmy,

00:00:42.908 --> 00:00:46.178
and they asked me if I'd like
to sit in the octagon.

00:00:46.178 --> 00:00:48.447
So, yeah, you know,

00:00:48.447 --> 00:00:50.517
there's a three-knockdown rule
now in first class.

00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:52.551
I don't know if
you know that, so...

00:00:52.551 --> 00:00:54.754
I should have rimshots for this,
don't you think?

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:56.322
-Yeah, we can get --
Quest can do a rimshot.

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:57.724
[ Rimshot ]
Yeah, of course.

00:00:57.724 --> 00:00:59.225
-Hey, last time I flew here,

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:00.592
the flight attendant
asked if I wanted

00:01:00.592 --> 00:01:01.928
headphones and duct tape.

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:04.563
[ Rimshot ]

00:01:04.563 --> 00:01:07.533
They stopped serving alcohol.
Now they serve Ambien.

00:01:07.533 --> 00:01:09.101
[ Rimshot ]
-Dude, the face.

00:01:09.101 --> 00:01:10.436
-Here's the last one.

00:01:10.436 --> 00:01:12.839
New slogan is, "There's
something special the air."

00:01:12.839 --> 00:01:15.007
-There you go.
-Yeah, MMA.

00:01:15.007 --> 00:01:17.043
-That's how you do
it, ladies and gentlemen.

00:01:17.043 --> 00:01:19.611
That's how you do it.
Write it down.

00:01:19.611 --> 00:01:21.047
Billy, you look great.

00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:22.748
But I heard you had
a little health scare.

00:01:22.748 --> 00:01:24.483
Is everything all right?

00:01:24.483 --> 00:01:26.385
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
That was just --

00:01:26.385 --> 00:01:30.856
You know, I've been working out
as much as I can,

00:01:30.856 --> 00:01:35.461
and so I did something
with my right hip.

00:01:35.461 --> 00:01:37.530
So it was just a strange pain.

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:40.967
So I was worried, 'cause
I don't want to join that

00:01:40.967 --> 00:01:42.768
"Yeah, I got a new hip" club.

00:01:42.768 --> 00:01:45.037
So, the doctor says,

00:01:45.037 --> 00:01:49.041
"Listen, I think the best thing
is to put you in the MRI tube,

00:01:49.041 --> 00:01:52.812
and, you know, let's take a
good look at your soft tissue."

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:56.949
So I said, "Fine, but I'm 73,
so this everything is soft

00:01:56.949 --> 00:01:58.317
at this point."

00:01:58.317 --> 00:02:00.286
-Nothing but soft tissue.

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:02.755
-You've been
in an MRI tube, right?

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:04.390
-Yeah.
-It's awful.

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:05.892
I mean, I'm very claustrophobic,

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:09.662
which is why
I was a month premature.

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:12.132
And, so...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:17.469
So, I get there and I'm nervous,

00:02:17.469 --> 00:02:18.905
and they shoot dye into the hip

00:02:18.905 --> 00:02:21.173
and then they put me
in the hospital gown,

00:02:21.173 --> 00:02:24.009
you know, with your ass
hangs out of the back.

00:02:24.009 --> 00:02:25.978
It's just --
Nothing is good about this.

00:02:25.978 --> 00:02:28.648
-Yeah, I feel like they need
to master that, yeah.

00:02:28.648 --> 00:02:30.182
-Yes, and I'm really nervous.

00:02:30.182 --> 00:02:32.684
So, to make a long story short,

00:02:32.684 --> 00:02:36.722
when I was alone, I swallowed
four edibles, alright?

00:02:36.722 --> 00:02:38.090
-Wait. What do you mean?

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:43.362
-Four, you know, edibles.
-Yeah, gummies.

00:02:43.362 --> 00:02:44.764
Wow.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:47.333
'Cause the guy
at the cannabis place said --

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:50.003
Because there's a section
for seniors, you know?

00:02:50.003 --> 00:02:52.939
So, he said,
"Two will make you feel good."

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:56.075
So I said, "Well,
I really want to feel fabulous."

00:02:56.075 --> 00:02:58.144
So he said to have four.
-So you had four gummies.

00:02:58.144 --> 00:03:00.480
-So, I swallow the four.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:03.916
So, now I get on the thing,
and they put me into the tube.

00:03:03.916 --> 00:03:06.018
And I have headsets on

00:03:06.018 --> 00:03:08.888
and I'm listening to
a little Bill Evans on Pandora.

00:03:08.888 --> 00:03:10.957
And they give you
this thing to squeeze,

00:03:10.957 --> 00:03:13.659
so in case you get into trouble,
you just squeeze it,

00:03:13.659 --> 00:03:14.727
and he says,
"What can I do?"

00:03:14.727 --> 00:03:16.429
and "I'll get you
out of there," right?

00:03:16.429 --> 00:03:21.901
So, about a half-hour in,
I got really hungry.

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:24.938
-Oh, my God.
You're a stoner now. Geez.

00:03:24.938 --> 00:03:26.539
-Yeah. And, so,
I squeeze the thing.

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:28.507
He goes,
"Are you okay, Mr. Crystal?"

00:03:28.507 --> 00:03:32.611
I said, "Yeah, yeah.
Is there a Taco Bell nearby?"

00:03:32.611 --> 00:03:34.213
-By the tube, is there any --
-Yeah. No?

00:03:34.213 --> 00:03:35.314
He said, "No."

00:03:35.314 --> 00:03:37.449
Alright. Alright.
Okay. Alright. Alright.

00:03:37.449 --> 00:03:39.752
Now, 40 minutes in, I squeezed
it again, and he goes,

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:40.753
"You're okay?"

00:03:40.753 --> 00:03:42.021
"Yeah. Yeah.

00:03:42.021 --> 00:03:45.525
I'm thinking if Postmates --
would they deliver?"

00:03:45.525 --> 00:03:46.992
-Just get me a taco.
Just get me something.

00:03:46.992 --> 00:03:48.127
Get me a burrito.

00:03:48.127 --> 00:03:51.096
-I'm thinking gumbo
or Nutella French toast,

00:03:51.096 --> 00:03:52.932
something like that.

00:03:52.932 --> 00:03:55.468
-You're a stoner.
You became a stoner.

00:03:55.468 --> 00:03:56.835
-In the tube.

00:03:56.835 --> 00:03:58.170
And I didn't want to
open my eyes,

00:03:58.170 --> 00:04:00.440
because I know, you know,
the roof is like right here.

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:01.940
-Yes.

00:04:01.940 --> 00:04:05.744
-So I'd feel like I was, like,
you know, a mummy or something.

00:04:05.744 --> 00:04:08.414
And, so, finally, I nodded off.

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:10.316
So it was like
1968 all over again,

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:12.485
so it's, like, very cool for me.

00:04:12.485 --> 00:04:15.221
So, they take me out,
and I walk out of the building.

00:04:15.221 --> 00:04:19.258
And someone says, "Um, sir,
you're still in your gown,

00:04:19.258 --> 00:04:21.060
and your ass is hanging out."

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:22.294
I said, "Oh, geez."

00:04:22.294 --> 00:04:26.065
So, I come back in,
I got dressed,

00:04:26.065 --> 00:04:30.103
and I went to a Taco Bell
and had a nacho fry box.

00:04:30.103 --> 00:04:31.637
-That's what I'm talking about.
See? Good.

00:04:31.637 --> 00:04:33.272
And everything worked out?

00:04:33.272 --> 00:04:36.041
-Yeah, I'm okay. I'm okay.

00:04:36.041 --> 00:04:37.943
-I wanted to mention,
once again,

00:04:37.943 --> 00:04:40.113
you're voicing Mike Wazowski.

00:04:40.113 --> 00:04:41.480
You're back.

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:44.350
Because we -- You know, in
"Monsters, Inc." and the sequel.

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:47.286
But now it's "Monsters at Work"
on Disney+.

00:04:47.286 --> 00:04:49.422
Any kid out there, any families
out there with kids,

00:04:49.422 --> 00:04:50.556
you have to watch this.

00:04:50.556 --> 00:04:52.291
You're fantastic.
-We're having a good time.

00:04:52.291 --> 00:04:54.794
It's John Goodman
and I and Mindy Kaling,

00:04:54.794 --> 00:04:56.428
Henry Winkler,

00:04:56.428 --> 00:04:59.131
a young, very talented actor
named Ben Feldman.

00:04:59.131 --> 00:05:01.033
So it's been a lot of fun.

00:05:01.033 --> 00:05:02.868
People seem to be
really liking it.

00:05:02.868 --> 00:05:06.972
It's a continuation of where
"Monsters, Inc." left off.

00:05:06.972 --> 00:05:08.441
So it's not a sequel.

00:05:08.441 --> 00:05:10.442
It's just a continuation
of the original story.

00:05:10.442 --> 00:05:11.844
20 years ago.

00:05:11.844 --> 00:05:15.214
This is the 20th anniversary of
"Monsters, Inc." Crazy.

00:05:15.214 --> 00:05:17.016
-That seems --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:17.016 --> 00:05:18.984
-That seems almost wrong.
That's why.

00:05:18.984 --> 00:05:20.286
It feels like it just came out.
-Yeah.

00:05:20.286 --> 00:05:22.889
This whole year is anniversaries
for me, though.

00:05:22.889 --> 00:05:26.426
It's the 30th anniversary
of "City Slickers."

00:05:26.426 --> 00:05:28.360
-Wow!
-Yeah, crazy.

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:30.530
And the 35th anniversary

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:33.632
of, really, my first role
that I really loved,

00:05:33.632 --> 00:05:36.468
and that was "Running Scared"
with the great Gregory Hines.

00:05:36.468 --> 00:05:37.736
-Oh, Gregory Hines. Absolutely.

00:05:37.736 --> 00:05:39.071
I love it.
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:05:39.071 --> 00:05:42.541
-Well, I love this new film that
you have, "Here Today."

00:05:42.541 --> 00:05:44.444
You wrote it. You directed it.

00:05:44.444 --> 00:05:46.245
You star in it
with Tiffany Haddish,

00:05:46.245 --> 00:05:47.613
who, by the way,
is fantastic, as well.

00:05:47.613 --> 00:05:48.781
-Yeah, she's great.

00:05:48.781 --> 00:05:53.819
-Why -- That's so much work.
I mean, that's...

00:05:53.819 --> 00:05:56.122
-Well, you know, it was
something that I really loved

00:05:56.122 --> 00:05:58.357
and I got to write it
with my dear friend

00:05:58.357 --> 00:06:00.426
and someone you know very well,
Alan Zweibel.

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:02.027
-I love Alan Zweibel.
He's a legend.

00:06:02.027 --> 00:06:06.832
-Yeah, And I saw him, actually,
on the "Letterman" show,

00:06:06.832 --> 00:06:10.803
telling this funny story
about how he met this person

00:06:10.803 --> 00:06:13.873
by chance
at a celebrity auction lunch.

00:06:13.873 --> 00:06:17.910
And she purchased him for $22,

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:21.614
and then she ended up having
an allergic reaction

00:06:21.614 --> 00:06:22.982
to the seafood she was eating.

00:06:22.982 --> 00:06:25.351
And she had no insurance.
She had to get an ambulance.

00:06:25.351 --> 00:06:29.889
And this charity lunch
cost him $3,000.

00:06:29.889 --> 00:06:31.323
-That's so funny.

00:06:31.323 --> 00:06:34.059
-So, I'm watching him,
Jim, and I said --

00:06:34.059 --> 00:06:35.495
And I started typing,

00:06:35.495 --> 00:06:37.029
"Alan, this is the beginning
of something.

00:06:37.029 --> 00:06:39.465
I don't know what it is,
but this is how they meet.

00:06:39.465 --> 00:06:41.267
Where do we go from there?"
And so on, so forth.

00:06:41.267 --> 00:06:45.237
So, we just started writing,
and it ended up becoming this,

00:06:45.237 --> 00:06:48.340
I think, really funny,
beautiful story

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:53.179
of these two mismatched
people who become great friends.

00:06:53.179 --> 00:06:56.048
-Yeah, it's very funny,
but it's also --

00:06:56.048 --> 00:06:58.850
It's got some very moving scenes
in there, too.

00:06:58.850 --> 00:06:59.886
Can I set it up or...

00:06:59.886 --> 00:07:01.420
-Sure.

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:04.390
-You're a writer
and suffering from dementia,

00:07:04.390 --> 00:07:05.891
the first stages of dementia.

00:07:05.891 --> 00:07:07.526
-Yes, I said, "Well, what if we

00:07:07.526 --> 00:07:09.228
complicate it
and he's got this?"

00:07:09.228 --> 00:07:12.798
Because the thought
of somebody funny,

00:07:12.798 --> 00:07:14.333
whose words are his currency,

00:07:14.333 --> 00:07:18.637
who's now going broke,
could be very dramatic

00:07:18.637 --> 00:07:21.807
and very fascinating to play.

00:07:21.807 --> 00:07:25.478
And can we put that into a movie
that we hope is funny,

00:07:25.478 --> 00:07:28.847
but also entertaining and
heartbreaking at the same time?

00:07:28.847 --> 00:07:31.551
And I'm very proud
of what we were able to do.

00:07:31.551 --> 00:07:34.353
-Yeah, and it's tricky
to come out with a movie

00:07:34.353 --> 00:07:37.089
during quarantine,
as well, but --

00:07:37.089 --> 00:07:39.058
-Well, yeah, I mean,
"Mom, come on, come on.

00:07:39.058 --> 00:07:40.693
We're going to go see
the dementia movie.

00:07:40.693 --> 00:07:42.961
Come on! Come on!"

00:07:42.961 --> 00:07:45.531
-Yeah, but, also --
But it's kind of good that

00:07:45.531 --> 00:07:46.699
it's out now
and it's streaming in --

00:07:46.699 --> 00:07:48.233
-Yeah, now people are --
I tell you,

00:07:48.233 --> 00:07:50.636
I mean, the reaction to it now,

00:07:50.636 --> 00:07:52.971
when people are
finally seeing it,

00:07:52.971 --> 00:07:55.408
has been really
heartwarming and great.

00:07:55.408 --> 00:07:57.643
And I thank everybody
who's now, you know,

00:07:57.643 --> 00:08:00.846
getting a chance to watch it,

00:08:00.846 --> 00:08:02.648
right, you know,
these last couple weeks.

00:08:02.648 --> 00:08:03.716
It's great.
-Well, you did a great job.

00:08:03.716 --> 00:08:05.684
And I love the --
There's a cameo of --

00:08:05.684 --> 00:08:09.021
Alan Zweibel's cameo as
the cue-card guy in the show.

00:08:09.021 --> 00:08:10.322
That made me laugh.
I just -- Yeah.

00:08:10.322 --> 00:08:13.959
If you talk to him,
well, tell him it was great.

00:08:13.959 --> 00:08:15.227
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:08:15.227 --> 00:08:17.830
Here's Billy Crystal and
Tiffany Haddish in "Here Today."

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:19.365
Take a look at this.

00:08:19.365 --> 00:08:21.333
-Thank you for bidding on me
in the auction.

00:08:21.333 --> 00:08:23.302
-Truth?
-Sure.

00:08:23.302 --> 00:08:25.704
-I don't know
who the hell you are.

00:08:25.704 --> 00:08:27.072
My ex bid on you.

00:08:27.072 --> 00:08:28.240
-How come your ex didn't come?

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:30.509
-I caught him cheating on me.
-Oh.

00:08:30.509 --> 00:08:32.144
-Yeah. And he said
it was because

00:08:32.144 --> 00:08:34.012
I'm the worst lay in the world

00:08:34.012 --> 00:08:37.016
And trust me --
he is wrong, okay?

00:08:37.016 --> 00:08:40.052
You ought to see my moves.
It's Cirque du Soleil.

00:08:40.052 --> 00:08:41.253
-Let's get through lunch first.

00:08:41.253 --> 00:08:42.888
-Mm-hmm.
I'd break your back, old man.

00:08:42.888 --> 00:08:44.323
-Thank you.

00:08:44.323 --> 00:08:46.826
-Yeah, have you laid out, dead,
with a smile on your face.

00:08:46.826 --> 00:08:47.960
-[ Laughs ]

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:50.362
-And your kids will be like,
"How did he die?

00:08:50.362 --> 00:08:51.864
How did my dad die?"

00:08:51.864 --> 00:08:53.865
And I would just have to look at
them in their eyes and say...

00:08:53.865 --> 00:08:55.668
[ Chuckles ]
..."On top of me."

00:08:59.605 --> 00:09:01.040
-That's a really lovely thought.

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:02.808
-[ Laughs ]

00:09:02.808 --> 00:09:04.376
"Thank you."
That was very good.

00:09:04.376 --> 00:09:06.111
Billy Crystal, everybody.

00:09:06.111 --> 00:09:08.147
I love it, buddy.
Please come back.

00:09:08.147 --> 00:09:10.316
Can't wait to see you in person.
-See you next time, Jimmy.

00:09:10.316 --> 00:09:13.519
-"Here Today" is available
now on digital Blu-ray and DVD.

